   "id": "b2_rank_unsigned_sibling_v1",
   "statement": "U_n(F) = the non-negative finite values of F's (n+1)-bit sibling, the sibling being F's encoding with one more least-significant bit and every other field and convention unchanged: float and MX elements one more mantissa bit (same exponent width, bias, subnormals, inf/NaN convention); logarithmic one more fractional exponent bit; BFP one more mantissa fraction bit; posit(n, es) -> posit(n+1, es). The sibling's sign bit is 0 and its other n bits are the unsigned code; ties go to the even code as in v1",
   "why": "for integers the rule gives exactly B2's unsigned integer codebook (non-negative half of INT(n+1)); it uses the freed sign bit for one more bit of resolution in every family",
